I must say, first of all, that this is the best and most polished
I must have played. The game lacks some features but it is far from empty and there is more content available than in many betas. And, most importantly, the features that are implemented do actually work correctly must of the time (the occasional glitch or bug does happen).
Pros:
Cartoonesque graphics do look awesome and do not punish performance;
Running people over is fun;
Simplistic crafting and building system (make complex structures with simple tools);
A decent amount of community servers and official servers;
Cons:
Too easy to get into an end-game state (get a car early and call it a good game);
Still no decent weapon recoil;
I highly recommend it.

People are giving this game negative reviews about it being sold on steam for 19.99€, since "they said the mod would be free for everyone! >:(". What they don't realize is that the mod is free for everyone, just go to their website. This is just the retail version.
Another thing fans don't like is that they stilll haven't had included Xen in. Which is understandable, although Xen was never a fan favourite location to begin with.
"Early Access" is there for a reason, you don't like it, don't buy it.
They still have some improvements to make (more details down below) but you gotta appreciate the effort they put into remaking one of the best (FPS) titles out there.
Some voice over still needs improvement (Eli Vance);
They sacrificed some elements people loved for the sake of realism, HECU Marines don't look like they did in Half-Life, instead they have been given more realistic appearances. Scientists and guards look like they've been based off the HD model pack, that one isn't that bad, can be fixed thanks to workshop. Would be nice to have the option in-game though;
Loading screens are pretty damn long, though nobody can really blame the devs for that, that's more of the engine's problem. Possible Source 2 port in the future could fix that (though they said they probably won't do that);
I might add more once I come up with some. If I missed anything, you can reply to it.
EDIT: There was some criticism where they cut some parts out, but they added On A Rail: Uncut to the workshop and Surface Tension: Uncut in the game. Now there's still Xen...

You heard right.  This is a totally free game, so unless you hate video games you probably should give it a quick download and at least check it out.
Now that that's out of the way.. yes, indeed, it's an RPGmaker game-- but don't let that turn you away.  Sure, it's got RPGmaker assets for most the backgrounds/terrain and some of the enemies, but;
- It's got fully custom character art for the main characters, with many different states as well as gorgeous full-screen art for many cutscenes;
- It's got REALLY nice custom music with only, like, 2 of the 20 or so songs in the game being anything approaching repetitive or grating, and several tracks being downright excellent;
- It's got a simple but beautiful and bittersweet story, especially once you get to the end;
- And best of all, it's got a hand-crafted action-RPG battle system reminiscent of the original Ys games and other oldschool RPGs instead of your regular random-battles-turn-based RPGmaker faire.
My only real complaint would be its length; as a free game made almost entirely by one guy, I wasn't expecting too much, but this lovely game is simply over far too quickly.  Even if you're the type like me that's going to go way out of your way to do absolutely every single optional thing possible and grind every item, you're still looking at a single afternoon's work all told.  The good news is the guy's apparently already hard at work on a sequel.
So yes, get this game, download it, play it, fill out the post-game survey, let the creator know he's a rad dude, and have a great time.  Sure, the gameplay's quite simple overall, it's not very long, and there are some generic graphical assets you MIGHT notice in between the gorgeous manga-style character art, but I can think of little excuse for anyone not to give this game a play.

