What i saw was a game about a vaccume and a bunch of slimes. What i expected was something about beaning wild animals(?) with food and collecting their defecation. What i got turned out to be spending most of the time broke, flying around in small intervals and cursing at everything when i fell into the ocean.
The good;
Your given a plot of land and some places to set up shop, its very straight forward and easy to understand. you get a few slimes in the starting aria and the game gives you all the time in their world to understand how to be a slime rancher. once you have the coins to buy upgrades to your vaccume, power and the jetpack than the world opens up and it becomes just as much about exploration as it does feeding your pens of slimes. Your time is either spend leasurly flying around exploring or franticly looking for food for your many hungry mouths.
The bad;
This game is linear in its paths and you will spend alot of time without coins to do anything. there is an infodump when you try to figure out how to optimise your production and profits and you'll end up losing crops. the game as a pseudo-story but doesnt really give you a direction so you must make your own objectives or be at a loss with all the options in this sandbox.
This is one of the few early access games i support and still play, its relaxing and frustrating and open and self contained and all around a good experiance.

